    <item>
      <title>Fused Filament Design Addon</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/fused-filament-design-addon/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 23 May 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/fused-filament-design-addon/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;A short while ago we posted here about an &lt;a href=&#34;https://blog.freecad.org/2025/05/08/design-for-3d-printing-an-excellent-article/&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;excellent article by Rahix describing some really interesting and useful design approaches for fused filament style 3D printing&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. If you haven&amp;rsquo;t checked out that article it&amp;rsquo;s really worth a read.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
